$DIR/main.p:29:10: cannot index r: method Index of owner type Reader has a value receiver, so the call would consume r
    An owner owns memory or another resource and releases it when it is dropped,
    so it moves instead of being copied. A method with a value receiver consumes
    its receiver: calling it moves the owner into the method, which drops it
    when it returns. r[k] and len(r) borrow the container for the call and never
    move it, so on an owner the methods they call take a pointer receiver.
    Declare the method with a pointer receiver:
        func (r *Reader) Index(k int) int
    (see "Indexing library containers" in the Plutonium spec, section 11.11)
    (run "pluto explain E2452" for a longer explanation)

